    <div class="cite-notes">
      <h3>Citing individual data points</h3>
      <p>Starrydata records are extracted from plot images in the original papers. When you reference an individual Sample or Curve in your own paper, please also cite the <strong>original source paper (CrossRef DOI)</strong>. Each curve's source DOI is available in the web system and in the <code>DOI</code> column of the dataset CSV.</p>

      <h3>Pinning a specific dataset version</h3>
      <p>For reproducibility, use one of the <strong>frozen dataset snapshots</strong> published on Figshare. Each snapshot carries a DOI per version so it can be cited permanently by version and retrieval date.</p>
      <ul class="cite-links">
        <li><a href="https://figshare.com/projects/Starrydata_datasets/155129" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Figshare — Starrydata datasets</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Permanent URL for the paper</h3>
      <p>The project paper (STAM:Methods 2025) is also archived on the NIMS Materials Data Repository (MDR), which guarantees a permanent URL — useful when you want to avoid link rot.</p>
      <ul class="cite-links">
        <li><a href="https://mdr.nims.go.jp/datasets/be1aaf76-761d-4b73-8ba4-f958348efade?locale=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NIMS MDR — Starrydata (paper archive)</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

